---
// SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
/** The Terms of Service, served at `/terms/`. */
import ContactLink from '@/components/legal/contact-link.astro';
import LegalPage from '@/components/legal/legal-page.astro';
---

<LegalPage
	title="Terms of Service"
	description="The terms for using SkillPouch, its command-line tool and its API."
	path="/terms/"
>
	<p>
		These terms apply when you use SkillPouch at skillpouch.net, its command-line tool and its
		API. By creating an account you agree to them.
	</p>

	<section>
		<h2>Your account</h2>
		<p>
			You sign in with GitHub or Google and are responsible for everything done with your
			account. Keep your master password and Recovery Key safe: your data is end-to-end
			encrypted, so if you lose both and have no other trusted device or browser, nobody,
			including us, can recover it.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Your content</h2>
		<p>
			You keep all rights to what you sync. You give us only the permission needed to store
			and deliver it, in encrypted form, to your devices and to the people you share it with.
			You are responsible for having the right to sync and share it.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Acceptable use</h2>
		<p>Do not use SkillPouch to:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>store or share anything illegal, or malware;</li>
			<li>infringe others’ rights;</li>
			<li>attack, overload or try to break into the service or other accounts;</li>
			<li>get around plan limits or resell the service without our permission.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>We may suspend accounts that break these rules.</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Plans and payments</h2>
		<p>
			The Free plan costs nothing. Paid plans are sold through Polar, our merchant of record,
			which handles payment, taxes and invoices. You can cancel at any time; your plan stays
			active until the end of the paid period. If you move to a smaller plan, nothing is
			deleted: anything above the new limits becomes read-only.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Availability</h2>
		<p>
			We work to keep SkillPouch available and your data safe, but the service is provided “as
			is”, without warranties. Your devices keep their own copies of your files; keep backups
			of anything important.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Liability</h2>
		<p>
			To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for indirect or consequential losses, or
			for loss of data. Our total liability is limited to the amount you paid us in the 12
			months before the claim.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Ending your account</h2>
		<p>
			You can delete your account at any time in your account settings. We may end or suspend
			accounts that break these terms, and will tell you why when we can.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Privacy</h2>
		<p>
			How we handle personal data is described in the <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Changes</h2>
		<p>
			We may update these terms. For significant changes we notify you before they take
			effect; using SkillPouch afterwards means you accept them.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Contact</h2>
		<p>
			Questions about these terms: <ContactLink />.
		</p>
	</section>
</LegalPage>
